WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.700
April's 27-B Open Model scores 98.9 on Big Bench Audio, while adding native speech and tool calling. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 222. Hyper Repair at inference cost,

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:21.420
agentic tuners for cosmology and safety, community builds, then things to try and on the horizon.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:28.980
Appreal Voice 27B Preview processes audio directly and outputs both text responses and toolcalls

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:35.840
without a separate dialogue model. Built on the post-trained Gemma 426 BA4B checkpoint,

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.900
the archive paper says it keeps text and image modalities. Training runs in two stages,

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:47.180
first establishing the speech interface, then jointly adapting the projector and backbone

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.720
with supervised fine-tuning, text replay and source dependent losses.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:01:01.220
In thinking mode, it reaches 81.13 on speech BFCL, and 65.51% task success on Tau voice

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.900
at 1.91 second mean latency.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:12.740
English EVA accuracy is 51.27%, and experience pass at 1 is 74.13%.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:16.960
The model runs on a custom-serving platform for interactive voice sessions.

00:01:17.967 --> 00:01:22.967
HyperRepair recovers general capabilities of fine-tune models at inference cost only.

00:01:23.607 --> 00:01:31.227
The framework trains a hyper network on source model repairs that generates a prompt-conditioned repairing side-net using activation fingerprints.

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:39.187
Tests ran on two model families, 12 low-rank adaptation, or Laura, data sets, and 15 general benchmarks.

00:01:39.187 --> 00:01:47.447
It retains 99.5% of domain performance. It recovers 93.4% of the base model's average

00:01:47.447 --> 00:01:52.987
general score. No target domain examples or extra optimization are required at inference.

00:01:54.228 --> 00:01:59.928
Patching the key value cache or KV cache from a lura-tuned model into the base transfers

00:01:59.928 --> 00:02:05.608
behaviors such as German response style or emergent misalignment. The reverse swap removes

00:02:05.608 --> 00:02:11.728
them. The effect concentrates at a few pivotal positions, especially system prompt and chat template

00:02:11.728 --> 00:02:18.691
tokens. It scales with the fraction of the cache replaced. Le2-SAO lifts single rollout asynchronous

00:02:18.691 --> 00:02:24.431
reinforcement learning with group relative actor critic bootstrapping. The method trains the actor

00:02:24.431 --> 00:02:29.651
with group relative advantage and the critic with group centered return, while the value model is

00:02:29.651 --> 00:02:36.451
cold, then switches to single roll out generalized advantage estimation, or G-A-E. It closes the early

00:02:36.451 --> 00:02:43.271
training gap with group relative policy optimization, or GRPO, on agentic tasks and raises the later

00:02:43.271 --> 00:02:50.154
performance ceiling. Code is released with the paper, auto regressive checkpoints from Gemma 29b,

00:02:50.714 --> 00:02:59.394
Lama 3.18b, Quinn 2.57b, and Ministeral 8b convert to diffusion language models under BYOD

00:02:59.394 --> 00:03:06.234
with Lora-only adapters. The recipe uses 4.1 to 5.8% of final parameters and at

00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:12.074
most 102.4 million tokens per conversion. All four models generate from fully

00:03:12.074 --> 00:03:17.514
mask sequences and retain substantial parent knowledge. BYOD Gemma reaches

00:03:17.514 --> 00:03:24.374
50.6% average accuracy on a 9-task suite. Tajik tool calling is the target of

00:03:24.374 --> 00:03:32.174
Zoda, Tajik, LFM, 2.6B, a hybrid model adapted with continued pre-training than supervised fine-tuning.

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:38.954
Laura continued pre-training ran on 1.48 million cleaned Tajik documents for three epochs,

00:03:39.274 --> 00:03:42.474
then one epoch of mixed tool-call supervised fine-tuning.

00:03:43.034 --> 00:03:52.174
Strict full-call accuracy on a 174 item Tajik BFCL derived test rose from 20.69 to 64.14.

00:03:52.174 --> 00:03:58.554
4. English tool-calling accuracy stays flat at approximately 77. Continued pre-training

00:03:58.554 --> 00:04:03.617
alone erases the native tool-call format. Cosmological simulations get

00:04:03.617 --> 00:04:08.057
agentic tuner, which uses a present-day large language model as the optimizer.

00:04:08.697 --> 00:04:13.497
The pipeline supplies informal human readable priors, code-based documentation,

00:04:13.977 --> 00:04:18.637
heuristics to the agent. It reaches competitive calibration performance at a

00:04:18.637 --> 00:04:21.297
of the CPU cost of Bayesian optimization.

00:04:22.385 --> 00:04:25.465
Safin 1.5 adds a safety native architecture

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:27.345
and a verifiable reasoning harness

00:04:27.345 --> 00:04:29.105
for recursive safety improvement.

00:04:29.725 --> 00:04:32.105
Persistent safety states and hazardous knowledge

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:35.485
disentanglement allow targeted removal of risky experts.

00:04:36.145 --> 00:04:37.465
The formal reasoning harness

00:04:37.465 --> 00:04:40.145
recovers missing relations via proof obligation

00:04:40.145 --> 00:04:41.685
guided semantic bridging

00:04:41.685 --> 00:04:45.425
and outperforms frontier models on safety and reasoning tasks.

00:04:45.425 --> 00:04:52.482
An ESP 32-based 4-inch screen now shows a B-top plus-plus-style terminal dashboard for

00:04:52.482 --> 00:04:56.302
a DGX cluster, according to a local LAA thread.

00:04:56.922 --> 00:05:02.942
Firmware is on GitHub with a Skill.MD file so agents can compile it, and a 3D-printed

00:05:02.942 --> 00:05:03.962
dock is in progress.

00:05:05.177 --> 00:05:09.017
Andre Carpathi posted a weekend hack called HackerTube on X.

00:05:09.017 --> 00:05:16.597
Clod filtered 43 million hacker news comments spanning 20 years down to 6454, repeatedly

00:05:16.597 --> 00:05:20.097
recommended videos, and built a YouTube-style site around them.

00:05:20.637 --> 00:05:25.857
Filtering dropped links, rejects, and spam, and only the remainder went to Sonnet with

00:05:25.857 --> 00:05:28.637
a CC workflow so it uses the sub-tokens.

00:05:29.117 --> 00:05:34.237
The data zip is public, state lives in the browser session with no login required, and

00:05:34.237 --> 00:05:37.197
the surviving comments under videos are the recommending ones.

00:05:37.197 --> 00:05:45.732
SimXAI adds a lightweight LLM centric conversational layer for existing explainable AI or XAI resources.

00:05:46.292 --> 00:05:51.972
A single tool calling LLM replaces separate intent, dialogue management and template modules.

00:05:52.472 --> 00:05:57.942
It improves task accuracy and reduces turns versus use style agents while preserving faithfulness.

00:05:58.732 --> 00:06:01.092
An evaluation code and data sets are released.

00:06:02.183 --> 00:06:06.483
Persona chat bench evaluates chat assistance across diverse simulated users.

00:06:06.483 --> 00:06:11.423
The benchmark pair's identical tasks with multiple persona cards that encode distinct

00:06:11.423 --> 00:06:12.503
needs and behaviors.

00:06:13.243 --> 00:06:18.143
Task performance and need fulfillment vary across personas, and strong aggregate scores

00:06:18.143 --> 00:06:22.043
do not guarantee consistent satisfaction of individual user requirements.

00:06:23.121 --> 00:06:28.761
From the pre-print stack, Kistas is a pre-registered portable fairness protocol measuring procedural

00:06:28.761 --> 00:06:34.381
symmetry, differential refusal, and stereotype reliance across matched counterfactual pairs

00:06:34.381 --> 00:06:37.041
for Iraqi social constituencies.

00:06:37.041 --> 00:06:39.741
Kofi breaks course-to-find diversity reward,

00:06:40.261 --> 00:06:42.061
applied only to successful attacks,

00:06:42.281 --> 00:06:45.861
yields 1.6 to 2.0 times more distinct strategies

00:06:45.861 --> 00:06:49.301
on harm bench, and 2.1 times higher diversity

00:06:49.301 --> 00:06:51.581
on ad bench versus the strongest baseline.

00:06:52.361 --> 00:06:56.521
Adaptive personalization work finds a 35% to 46% drop

00:06:56.521 --> 00:06:59.421
in strategy calibration during open-ended generation

00:06:59.421 --> 00:07:01.501
versus multiple choice recognition.

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:06.801
With targeted training on internal strategy representations, narrowing the generalization

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:12.681
gap by one-third, better retrievers raise the share of no-gold context that still contain

00:07:12.681 --> 00:07:22.021
the answer from 28% to 72%, dropping shortcut precision from 0.68 to 0.10 in conversational

00:07:22.021 --> 00:07:23.481
rag abstention evaluation.

00:07:24.501 --> 00:07:33.861
Zeroing 729 task redundant heads in GPT-2 XL cuts memorization count by 91.5% while improving

00:07:33.861 --> 00:07:37.501
wiki text 103 perplexity by 0.92.

00:07:38.241 --> 00:07:45.061
On Bilal bench, six of seven evaluated open language models confidently fabricate on 79.3

00:07:45.201 --> 00:07:49.421
to 95.3% of source production questions in Bengali.

00:07:49.421 --> 00:07:58.721
Langflow outperforms D-Spark variants on GenPPL and MOV at lengths 128 and 1,024 under equal

00:07:58.721 --> 00:07:59.621
training budgets.

00:08:00.161 --> 00:08:07.301
Trace spec raises replay throughput 12.5 to 22.6% over its D-Spark base across three target

00:08:07.301 --> 00:08:14.821
sizes, with adaptive allocation increasing accepted length 3.3 to 10.0% over fixed full-turn

00:08:14.821 --> 00:08:21.841
supervision. AICG reduces mean absolute error by 50.3% and lifts quadratic-weighted

00:08:21.841 --> 00:08:29.521
Kappa from 0.798 to 0.927 versus plain Roberta regression for mathematical short answer

00:08:29.521 --> 00:08:34.701
grading. Psy interviewE keeps clinical facts fixed with asymmetric right permissions

00:08:34.701 --> 00:08:40.481
while disclosure and behavioral states evolve, and it outperforms four baselines on informational

00:08:40.481 --> 00:08:42.761
invariance and relational adaptivity.

00:08:43.441 --> 00:08:49.001
ASTC uses native recurrent dynamics to carry absorbed information forward as soft tokens,

00:08:49.621 --> 00:08:55.841
cutting end-to-end attention pairs by up to 50.68% while matching uncompressed accuracy.

00:08:56.541 --> 00:09:01.701
GSR Bench introduces a four-level hierarchy of reformulation capabilities for grounded

00:09:01.701 --> 00:09:07.161
generative speech recognition and finds acoustic hallucination and instruction drift as key

00:09:07.161 --> 00:09:07.921
failure modes.

00:09:07.921 --> 00:09:13.441
Direct absolute rating matches comparative ranking on rank correlation with human scores

00:09:13.441 --> 00:09:19.081
for academic paper quality, yet abstract only input beats full paper summarization.

00:09:19.621 --> 00:09:25.861
Blind to change shows a 27.5 point gap when a needed fact is not explicitly mentioned

00:09:25.861 --> 00:09:30.601
and more than half of failures trace to agents never searching to verify assumptions.

00:09:31.201 --> 00:09:36.281
Keeper finds reward-related prediction yields the highest task performance before and after

00:09:36.281 --> 00:09:42.001
offline RL, with claim-level analysis showing error persistence despite corrective observations.

00:09:42.601 --> 00:09:48.361
A dual-budget sparse text diffusion configuration cuts costs 20% relative to diffuse seek

00:09:48.361 --> 00:09:55.921
under the reported timing. Laura adapted T5 reaches the highest macro F1 of 0.7408

00:09:55.921 --> 00:10:01.921
on abstracts and 0.7013 on full text for knowledge entity relation extraction.

00:10:01.921 --> 00:10:08.241
Focal loss plus supervised contrast of learning outperformed strong baselines on sentence and document

00:10:08.241 --> 00:10:14.601
level CEFR prediction in both monolingual and multilingual settings. A second complementary

00:10:14.601 --> 00:10:20.541
steering vector restores approximately 78% of unintended discourse changes while preserving

00:10:20.541 --> 00:10:26.721
93% of the intended behavior. The repetition penalty parameter alone enables controllable

00:10:26.721 --> 00:10:31.461
precision recall adjustment at inference time for grammatical error correction without

00:10:31.461 --> 00:10:33.181
architecture or prompt changes.

00:10:33.661 --> 00:10:42.361
On Graf Nia at depth 16 and 32, GPT 5.6 and Qwen 3.5 models answer yes, no questions, no

00:10:42.361 --> 00:10:45.081
better than random, mostly by answering no.

00:10:45.681 --> 00:10:50.621
Stepwise queering distills reasoning without teacher chain of thought access and wins 14

00:10:50.621 --> 00:10:55.261
of 16 comparisons across two teachers, two students and four benchmarks.

00:10:55.261 --> 00:11:06.301
Peele recovers taxonomic directed acyclic graphs with high structural fidelity on two OLLM benchmarks using only a concept vocabulary from Matryoshka embeddings.

00:11:06.941 --> 00:11:14.241
Depth two path signatures optimally balanced character and word level sensitivities and preserve word order for lexical similarity.

00:11:15.681 --> 00:11:21.981
TIZSKT achieves the highest mean AUC and accuracy on all target domains in leave one domain

00:11:21.981 --> 00:11:25.161
out tests by using text only as an index.

00:11:25.781 --> 00:11:31.641
A 66-dimensional embedding space derived from 4.7 million human-odd one-out judgments

00:11:32.201 --> 00:11:38.341
supplies dimension-grounded rationales, and RSA on an FMRI data set shows increased human

00:11:38.341 --> 00:11:40.161
model representational alignment.

00:11:40.161 --> 00:11:52.221
Turn-Turk GPT predicts turn-taking in Turkish from text and beats both rule baselines and a multi-lingual end-of-turn detector under recording disjoint and speaker disjoint evaluation.

00:11:52.861 --> 00:12:01.261
Distilled asynchronous flow map language models set new state-of-the-art one-step performance on Sudoku and GSM 8K code generation.

00:12:02.121 --> 00:12:09.461
CROS raises out-of-domain accuracy to 46.8% on reasoning gym by scrambling chain-of-thought-step

00:12:09.461 --> 00:12:16.101
order while preserving content. Range SWA enables training-free length extrapolation for continuous

00:12:16.101 --> 00:12:21.521
diffusion language models with local sliding window attention, remote block summaries,

00:12:21.761 --> 00:12:28.541
and dynamic retrieval. ZHA grows a tree of compressed key summaries, so total cost grows sublinearly

00:12:28.541 --> 00:12:34.521
in sequence length, while preserving long-context retrieval after a short KL distillation stage.

00:12:34.981 --> 00:12:42.741
The 1.7B decision-ranked model beats its 27B generative teacher on Trek-DL19 through 23.

00:12:43.341 --> 00:12:50.021
Flight answers queries up to 9.5 times faster than VLLM and SG-Lang while staying closest

00:12:50.021 --> 00:12:51.461
to float 32 reference.

00:12:52.181 --> 00:12:57.301
A matched query protocol with content-based labeling shows that rag-defense ranking shift

00:12:57.301 --> 00:13:00.101
when prevented versus introduced failures are distinguished.

00:13:01.081 --> 00:13:06.141
Farrow's equal risk contribution variant lowers clean data loss on every seed by an average

00:13:06.141 --> 00:13:10.521
0.0136 NATS, with no added time or memory.

00:13:11.553 --> 00:13:15.833
Test app-real-voice 27B on speech-conditioned tool-calling tasks.

00:13:16.233 --> 00:13:19.893
The two-stage recipe is fully described, and the model is open.

00:13:20.593 --> 00:13:25.213
Run the hacker-tube data zip through your own agent to generate a personalized video feed

00:13:25.213 --> 00:13:29.713
filtered by topic or error. Compare hyper-repair against standard

00:13:29.713 --> 00:13:35.993
Laura reversal on any fine-tuned 7B to 13B model you already have. The hyper-network

00:13:35.993 --> 00:13:41.773
checkpoint is released. Apply KV-Cache patching to a safety-tuned model to see

00:13:41.773 --> 00:13:46.615
how much of the alignment behavior transfers without retraining. More open

00:13:46.615 --> 00:13:51.135
speech-language models are expected to adopt the two-stage projector plus backbone

00:13:51.135 --> 00:13:53.095
recipe demonstrated by app real.

00:13:53.875 --> 00:13:58.715
Agentec calibration pipelines like Agentec tuner will likely appear for other scientific

00:13:58.715 --> 00:14:00.615
simulators beyond cosmology.

00:14:01.335 --> 00:14:06.435
Portable fairness protocols modeled on keystas are anticipated for additional languages and

00:14:06.435 --> 00:14:07.755
regulatory jurisdictions.

00:14:08.415 --> 00:14:15.495
67.6% average accuracy at 4 billion is why we pop the hood on EDU Jev's pointer heads

00:14:15.495 --> 00:14:17.695
for single-pass categorical decisions.

00:14:18.624 --> 00:14:23.724
Pointerheads let a model output a probability distribution over a fixed set of options in

00:14:23.724 --> 00:14:29.104
one forward pass by scoring each option with a learned marker instead of generating tokens.

00:14:29.764 --> 00:14:35.364
The core move is to replace the usual language modeling head with a small set of option-specific

00:14:35.364 --> 00:14:37.624
linear probes that share the same encoder.

00:14:38.104 --> 00:14:43.724
Because the output vocabulary is now exactly the allowed choices, calibration becomes a direct

00:14:43.724 --> 00:14:48.464
softmax over those scores rather than an indirect mapping from freeform text.

00:14:48.684 --> 00:14:53.484
That removes both the parsing step and the risk that the model produces an out-of-set answer.

00:14:54.414 --> 00:15:00.034
The family supplies single-pass decision models from 0.8 billion to 4 billion for education

00:15:00.034 --> 00:15:00.634
tasks.

00:15:01.154 --> 00:15:08.754
The 4B variant hits 67.6% average accuracy across 12 education benchmarks, beating the strongest

00:15:08.754 --> 00:15:17.014
commercial API by 9.4 points, and the best open 4B model by 18.7 points. It runs approximately

00:15:17.014 --> 00:15:23.874
150 decisions per second on 1H100, roughly an order of magnitude faster than any text generation

00:15:23.874 --> 00:15:29.994
baseline that must be post-processed. The quality gain disappears once the option set grows beyond

00:15:29.994 --> 00:15:34.814
a few hundred entries, because the pointer head must still compete with the encoder's capacity.

00:15:34.814 --> 00:15:40.094
At that scale, a lightweight re-ranker on top of a generative model becomes preferable.

00:15:40.574 --> 00:15:45.554
Use pointer heads when the task is closed set classification with a stable label inventory

00:15:45.554 --> 00:15:46.754
and latency matters.

00:15:47.394 --> 00:15:52.274
Fall back to generation plus parsing when the label space is open or changes frequently.

00:15:53.208 --> 00:15:58.848
Before we go, decision model re-rankers trained with item space on policy distillation are expected

00:15:58.848 --> 00:16:00.828
to target additional retrieval benchmarks.

00:16:01.468 --> 00:16:03.288
That's models and agents for today.

